# Lumen Bay Curbside Composting Program: Performance Synthesis

**Scope:** participation, landfill diversion, cost per household and resident satisfaction. Both agents returned `status: partial`. All figures refer to 2025 unless stated otherwise.

## Established

Each figure below appears in two sources. However, the Gazette says it is reporting "city sign-up figures," so it likely relays the same council data rather than measuring anything itself. These figures agree across sources, but they may not be independently verified.

- **41% of households signed up for curbside composting in 2025.** This counts registrations, not active use.
  - [Lumen Bay City Council - Annual Waste Report 2025](doc://council-waste-report-2025, 2026-01-15): "Registered participation: 41% of households (sign-ups as of Dec 2025)."
  - [Lumen Bay Gazette](https://lumenbay-gazette.example/2026/03/composting-milestone, 2026-03-10): "reached 41% of households in 2025, according to city sign-up figures."
- **About 12,000 tonnes of food waste diverted from landfill in 2025.**
  - [Lumen Bay City Council - Annual Waste Report 2025](doc://council-waste-report-2025, 2026-01-15): "Food waste diverted from landfill: 12,000 tonnes."
  - [Lumen Bay Gazette](https://lumenbay-gazette.example/2026/03/composting-milestone, 2026-03-10): "diverted roughly 12,000 tonnes of food waste from the Harrow Point landfill." The Gazette is the only source that names the Harrow Point landfill.

## Contested

### Participation: 41% vs. 34%

| Value | What it measures | Source | Date |
|---|---|---|---|
| 41% of households | Households registered or signed up (as of Dec 2025) | [Lumen Bay City Council - Annual Waste Report 2025](doc://council-waste-report-2025, 2026-01-15) | 2026-01-15 |
| 41% of households | City sign-up figures, as reported in the press | [Lumen Bay Gazette](https://lumenbay-gazette.example/2026/03/composting-milestone, 2026-03-10) | 2026-03-10 |
| 34% of households | Households actively using bins at least twice a month, from a door-to-door survey of 1,200 households | [Coastal Sustainability Institute](https://coastal-sustainability.example/reports/lumen-bay-2025, 2026-02-01) | 2026-02-01 |

**Likely reason:** the two figures use different methods and measure different things.
- The 41% comes from administrative sign-up records.
- The 34% comes from a sample survey of observed active use, with a threshold of at least twice a month.
- The Institute says "Sign-up counts overstate active use because many registered households never set a bin out."

The figures are not necessarily in conflict. Enrollment and active use are different measures. Neither is preferred here.

### Cost per household: $18 vs. $21 per year

| Value | Basis | Source | Date |
|---|---|---|---|
| About $18 per household per year | A blog's reading of the **2024** municipal budget (secondary, non-official) | [GreenLedger (blog)](https://greenledger-blog.example/posts/lumen-bay-compost-costs, 2025-11-05) | 2025-11-05 |
| $21 per household per year | Official **2025** budget figure in the council's annual report | [Lumen Bay City Council - Annual Waste Report 2025](doc://council-waste-report-2025, 2026-01-15) | 2026-01-15 |

**Likely reason:** the figures cover different budget years and come from different kinds of source.
- The council report says the 2025 cost is "up from 2024 due to a new collection route." This fits with a lower 2024 figure.
- The council report does not state the 2024 figure, so the blog's $18 cannot be confirmed against it.
- The unread hauler contract memo (see Coverage gaps) may affect either figure.

## Single-source

- **72% satisfaction.** "72% of composting participants rated the program 'satisfied' or 'very satisfied'." Source: [Resident Services Survey - Summary of Results](doc://resident-survey-summary, 2026-02-20). This counts participants only. Non-participants' views are not covered.
- **Summer odour complaint.** The most common complaint was "odour from bins in summer (cited by 22%)." Source: [Resident Services Survey - Summary of Results](doc://resident-survey-summary, 2026-02-20). The summary does not say whether the 22% is a share of participants or of all respondents.
- **34% active use** (survey of 1,200 households). Source: [Coastal Sustainability Institute](https://coastal-sustainability.example/reports/lumen-bay-2025, 2026-02-01). This figure also appears under Contested.
- **$18 per household per year** (based on the 2024 budget). Source: [GreenLedger (blog)](https://greenledger-blog.example/posts/lumen-bay-compost-costs, 2025-11-05). This figure also appears under Contested.
- **$21 per household per year in 2025, higher than 2024 because a new collection route was added.** Source: [Lumen Bay City Council - Annual Waste Report 2025](doc://council-waste-report-2025, 2026-01-15). This figure also appears under Contested.

## Coverage gaps

### Error objects reported by agents

1. **web_researcher: `no_results`** (`isRetryable: false`)
   - The searches "Lumen Bay composting resident satisfaction" and "Lumen Bay compost complaints survey" returned no sources on satisfaction, complaints or feedback.
   - The searches themselves did not fail.
   - The only survey found (Coastal Sustainability Institute) measured how often bins were used, not satisfaction.
   - As a result, no public or web source supports the satisfaction figures. The only satisfaction evidence comes from the internal resident survey document.
2. **doc_analyst: `timeout`** (`isRetryable: true`)
   - `read_document doc_id=hauler-contract-memo` ("Memo: Organics Hauler Contract Renewal", 2026-03-02) timed out after 2.0s on both the first try and the retry.
   - The memo may contain cost or contract figures, so **the cost-per-household findings may be incomplete** and could be revised by it.
   - The agent read only 2 of 3 documents. The memo could not be checked against the other figures.
   - A later retry may succeed.

### What is missing by sub-topic

- **Participation**
  - There is no official set-out or active-use rate. The 34% comes only from a third-party survey.
  - No figures for other years were found, so no trend can be established.
- **Landfill diversion**
  - Only a tonnage total is available.
  - There is no diversion rate, no share of the total waste stream, no baseline and no year-over-year change.
- **Cost per household**
  - No official 2024 figure was found, so the size of the 2024-to-2025 increase is unknown.
  - There is no fee schedule and no data for 2025-26 onward.
  - The hauler contract memo has not been read.
- **Resident satisfaction**
  - All evidence comes from one internal survey summary.
  - There is no sample size, no trend, no complete complaint breakdown, and no data on non-participants.
  - The denominator for the 22% figure is not stated.
- **Source diversity**
  - Five web searches returned only three distinct sources.
  - The "established" figures probably trace back to a single city dataset.

### Overall judgment

Both agents concluded that the evidence does not support a reliable overall judgment of how well the program is performing. This report does not offer one.
